{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Behold, etc.</b> There is no need for a person to behold the king of Assyria, only behold Zion:" "<b>The city of our appointed feasts.</b> As its plain meaning, or like \"they burned all the meeting places of El\" <small>(Psalms 74:8)</small>:" "<b>Tent.</b> Deficient [in spelling], [lacking] a vav." "<b>Will not be removed.</b> It has no cognate [parallel form], and its meaning is \"will not fall,\" or \"he will not pull up its pegs\" — tent-peg among tent-pegs:" "<b>And all.</b> The cords are the strings:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:35.919319234Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}